  "_comment": "Opt-in multi-candidate specialization/voting gateway for jev_mcp.py's jev_ask tool. Copy to a real path and point JEV_ROUTES_FILE at it; absent entirely, jev_ask behaves exactly as today (single configured endpoint, no routing). Each route key is a 'decision_type' a caller can pass to jev_ask; candidates reuse the same record shape detect_jev_records() produces in claude-providers.sh (provider_id, base_url, key_var, model) so a route candidate can be lifted straight from 'claude-providers list'. min_confidence gates a single candidate's trust; min_agreement (optional) additionally requires >=2 candidates to independently agree on the same answer before the gateway trusts it -- when they disagree, the gateway degrades honestly (reports degraded:true, agreement:false) rather than silently picking one.",
